<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss govt sets terms on latest federal bond.</title>
<headline>Swiss govt sets terms on latest federal bond.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The terms were set on the latest issue by the Swiss federal government, which comprises a reopening of the outstanding government 4-1/2 percent June 2007 Confederate bond. The bond is priced at 105.45 to yield 3.849 percent per annumn.</p>
<p>BORROWER - Swiss Government</p>
<p> AMT   = 904 MLN CHF  COUPON	4.50     MATURITY   10.JUN.07</p>
<p> TYPE   fixed-rate    ISS PRICE  105.45    SETTLEMENT 06.FEB.97</p>
<p> YLD   = 3.849 PCT    FUNGIBLE WITH = VALOR NR 470 458</p>
<p> PROVISIONAL VALOR NR = 576 917</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
